er than writing to middleware)TjT*-0.0005 Tc-0.05 Tw(APIs \(which is the old CORBA style of distributed object computing\), your com-)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0033 Tw(ponents gain middleware services )Tj/F13 1 Tf15.2381 0 TD-0.0036 Tw(implicitly and transparently)Tj/F11 1 Tf13.0476 0 TD0.0034 Tc-0.0028 Tw( from the EJB)Tj-28.2857 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc0.0313 Tw[(server)-16.5(, without writing one line of middleware code yourself. The application)]TJT*0.0016 Tc-0.05 Tw(server implicitly handles transactions, persistence, security, state management,)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0004 Tw(component lifecycle, threading, and more.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD0.0139 Tc0.0626 Tw[(The cross-platform, cross-vendor nature of the EJB standard is another ex-)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0006 Tc-0.05 Tw(tremely important benefit that EJB brings to the table. It means that there\325s now)TjT*-0.0101 Tc-0.0499 Tw(a common standard for distributed component architectures to which all vendors)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.0108 Tw[(can integrate. It also means that there\325)-37.1(s going to be intense competition in the)]TJT*0.0293 Tw[(EJB market. EJB levels the playing field by defining one standard component)]TJT*0.004 Tc0.0049 Tw(API. This means you can expect the new EJB-compliant products that emerge)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0498 Tw(in the market to be both reliable and high-performing because middleware ven-)TjT*0.0067 Tc0.0625 Tw(dors can be compared in the same light. There is one standard, allowing the)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0361 Tw(vendors to focus on the quality of their EJB products. The standard also allows)TjT*-0.0082 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(application developers to focus on writing best-of-breed applications, rather than)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0 Tw(supporting every brand of middleware out there. This is the promise of EJB.)Tj/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 67 155 Tm0 Tc0.0004 Tw[(Remote Method Invocation \(R)-55.1(M)28.1(I\) and R)-56.2(M)-46(I-I)38.2(IOP)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 134 Tm0.0039 Tc0.0421 Tw[(The EJB standard depends on several other APIs in J2EE; the most visible of)]TJT*-0.0259 Tw[(these is Java Remote Method Invocation \(RMI\). RMI is a mechanism for invok-)]TJT*0.0194 Tw[(ing methods remotely on other machines. It is tightly integrated with the Java)]TJT*0.0415 Tw[(language itself; if you know Java, it won\325t take much to learn RMI. EJB relies)]TJT*0.0002 Tw(on RMI as a communications API between components and their clients.)Tj0 -1.8095 TD-0.0036 Tc-0.05 Tw[(RMI is seamless\321you almost don\325)-35.3(t even know you\325re using it when you program)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc-0.038 Tw[(your distributed application. RMI allows Java programmers to communicate in)]TJETendstreamendobj201 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj203 0 obj<</Length 4572>>stream
