tten and main-)]TJT*-0.0001 Tw(tained by non-Java savvy staff members \(JSPs do not require a Java compiler\).)Tj0 -1.8095 TD0.0039 Tc0 Tw[(W)35.8(e)0( illustrate connecting servlets with EJB components in Chapters 12 and 15.)]TJ/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 67 347 Tm0.0004 Tc0.001 Tw[(Java I)-81.3(D)0.2(L)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 326 Tm0.004 Tc0.0049 Tw(As we\325ve mentioned, CORBA is a massive middleware effort developed by the)Tj0 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc0.0455 Tw[(Object Management Group \(OMG\). The OMG represents hundreds of compa-)]TJT*-0.0158 Tw[(nies that have invested in this cross-platform architecture. CORBA is language)]TJT*0.0392 Tw[(independent; it doesn\325t matter what you code your programs in with CORBA,)]TJT*0.0001 Tw(so long as CORBA supports the language in which you\325re developing.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD-0.0061 Tc-0.0059 Tw[(Java IDL is an implementation of the CORBA specification in Java, and it allows)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD-0.0484 Tw[(for connectivity and interoperability with heterogeneous objects. Java IDL is one)]TJT*0.0219 Tw[(specific implementation of CORBA; there are many such implementations. And)]TJT*0.018 Tw[(while Java IDL does not implement everything that is specified in CORBA, Java)]TJT*-0.0098 Tw[(IDL ships free with the Java 2 platform. W)-28.5(e)0( cover Java IDL briefly in Chapter 11.)]TJ/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 67 171 Tm0.0003 Tc(JavaMail)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 150 Tm0.0116 Tc[(Sun\325)31.6(s )]TJ/F13 1 Tf2.6667 0 TD0.0124 Tc0.0695 Tw(JavaMail API)Tj/F11 1 Tf6.381 0 TD0.0116 Tc0.0625 Tw[( allows your applications to use e-mail capabilities. The)]TJ-9.0476 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc0.0033 Tw(JavaMail object model is quite simple to use, and it is easy to pick up if you\325ve)TjT*-0.0207 Tw[(been programming with Java \(it follows similar methodologies, such as excep-)]TJT*-0.0087 Tc-0.05 Tw[(tion handling and event handling\). Like most of the other J2EE APIs \(JNDI comes)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0067 Tw[(to mind\), JavaMail defines a set of interfaces to which you write your applica-)]TJT*-0.0137 Tw[(tion code, and those interfaces shield your code from the specific protocols or)]TJT*-0.0018 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(mail service implementations used. Y)-12.9(our Internet mail code effectively becomes)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0451 Tw[(portable across platforms, as well as across mail protocols. JavaMail also ships)]TJETendstreamendobj220 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj222 0 obj<</Length 5219>>stream
