66 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(functionality that can be assembled to form larger applications. Enterprise beans)]TJ/F13 1 TfT*-0.0004 Tc(may)Tj/F11 1 Tf2 0 TD0.0001 Tc-0.05 Tw[( also be reusable components, but this is not guaranteed. Don\325)-43.9(t believe any-)]TJ-2 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc-0.0299 Tw(one who tells you that enterprise beans are reusable by definition because that)TjT*(is )Tj/F13 1 Tf1.0476 0 TD(false)Tj/F11 1 Tf2.0952 0 TD0.0332 Tw[(. Y)108.3(ou need to design your beans correctly if you want them to be reus-)]TJ-3.1429 -1.2381 TD-0.0024 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(able. Y)21.5(ou need to consider the different applications, domains, and users of your)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0006 Tw(enterprise beans, and you need to develop your beans with as much flexibility)TjT*0.0607 Tw[(as possible. Developing a truly reusable set of beans will likely require many)]TJT*-0.0024 Tc-0.05 Tw[(iterations of feedback from customers using your beans in real-world situations.)]TJ0 -1.9048 TD0.0039 Tc0.0003 Tw(Roughly speaking, bean reusability can fall into three different levels:)Tj/F22 1 Tf0 -1.8095 TD0.021 Tw(Reuse as given.)Tj/F11 1 Tf8 0 TD0.0183 Tw(The application assembler uses the acquired bean as it is to)Tj-6.9524 -1.2381 TD0.0148 Tw[(build an application. The bean functionality cannot be tailored to fit the ap-)]TJT*0.0002 Tw(plication. This is typically what bean providers are offering in the market.)Tj/F22 1 Tf-1.0476 -1.619 TD-0.0372 Tw(Reuse by customization.)Tj/F11 1 Tf12.2857 0 TD-0.0324 Tw(The application assembler configures the acquired)Tj-11.2381 -1.2381 TD0.0185 Tw(bean by modifying the bean properties to fit the specific needs of the appli-)TjT*-0.0198 Tw[(cation. Bean customization typically occurs during development time. T)25.9(o)0( al-)]TJT*-0.0018 Tc-0.05 Tw[(low for a more flexible maintenance environment, some bean providers allow)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0006 Tw(runtime bean customization.)Tj/F22 1 Tf-1.04