Tw(the bean itself acts as a client)Tj/F22 1 Tf13.0476 0 TD0 Tc0 Tw( )Tj/F11 1 Tf0.2857 0 TD0.0039 Tc0.0094 Tw(and contacts another bean\321a verifier bean\321to)Tj-13.3333 -1.2381 TD0.0015 Tc-0.05 Tw(verify your credit rating. Once your credit is verified, the original bean can com-)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.0339 Tw[(plete the transaction. So beans can indeed be clients of other beans. This is a)]TJT*-0.0454 Tw[(very powerful, flexible model, and it allows for large-grained components to be)]TJT*-0.0002 Tw(composed of smaller ones in a hierarchical fashion.)Tj/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 67 301 Tm0.0001 Tc-0.0001 Tw[(The EJ)-69.8(B Server and EJ)34.7(B Container Providers)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 280 Tm0.0039 Tc0.0073 Tw[(If you\325ll recall, an application server provides middleware services to your ap-)]TJT*0.0083 Tc0.0625 Tw(plications, such as transaction services, security services, and others. These)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.007 Tw[(services are needed for your application to be scalable, robust, and secure for)]TJT*-0.0327 Tw[(multiple concurrent users. EJB takes the notion of application servers and par)-32.4(-)]TJT*-0.0001 Tw(titions them into two distinct parts:)Tj/F22 1 Tf0 -1.8095 TD0.0022 Tc-0.0573 Tw[(The EJB container)27.6(.)]TJ/F11 1 Tf9.7143 0 TD0.0024 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(The EJB container provides a playground where your en-)]TJ-8.6667 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc-0.0375 Tw[(terprise beans can run. There can be many beans running within a container)-5.8(.)]TJT*-0.0018 Tc-0.0499 Tw(Bean containers are responsible for managing the beans running within them.)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0367 Tw(They interact with the beans by calling a few required methods that the bean)TjT*0.0001 Tw(must expose. Containers may also provide access to a legacy system.)Tj/F22 1 Tf-1.0476 -1.619 TD0.0344 Tw[(The EJB server)63.6(.)]TJ/F11 1 Tf8.2857 0 TD0.03 Tw(The EJB server provides a runtime environment for one or)Tj-7.2381 -1.2381 TD-0