*-0.0046 Tw[(actions and how you can use them effectively in Chapter 10. For now)64.7(, know)]TJT*-0.0478 Tw(that the EJB server provides a )Tj/F13 1 Tf13.2381 0 TD-0.0531 Tw(transaction service)Tj/F11 1 Tf8.6667 0 TD-0.0478 Tw[(\321a low-level implementa-)]TJ-21.9048 -1.2381 TD0.0052 Tc0.0626 Tw[(tion of transaction management and coordination. The transaction service)]TJT*0.0024 Tc-0.05 Tw(must be exposed through the )Tj/F13 1 Tf12.8571 0 TD0.0022 Tc-0.0555 Tw[(Java T)101.5(ransaction API)]TJ/F11 1 Tf9.7143 0 TD-0.0476 Tc0 Tw( \()Tj/F13 1 Tf0.5714 0 TD0.0022 Tc[(JT)67.8(A)]TJ/F11 1 Tf1.7143 0 TD0.0024 Tc-0.05 Tw[(\). The JT)68.3(A is a high-)]TJ-24.8571 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc-0.0216 Tw[(level interface that you can use to control transactions, which we also cover)]TJT*0.001 Tw(in Chapter 10.)Tj/F22 1 Tf-1.0476 -1.619 TD-0.0048 Tc-0.0574 Tw[(Implicit security)41.1(.)]TJ/F11 1 Tf8.5714 0 TD-0.0037 Tc-0.05 Tw(Security is a major consideration for multi-tier deployments.)Tj-7.5238 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc0.0556 Tw(The Java 2 Platform, Standard Edition yields a robust security service that)TjT*-0.016 Tw[(can authorize and authenticate users, securing deployments from unwanted)]TJT*-0.0424 Tw[(visitors. EJB adds to this the notion of transparent security)58.6(, allowing compo-)]TJT*0.0433 Tw(nents to reap the benefits of a secure deployment without necessarily cod-)TjT*0.0002 Tw(ing to a security API.)Tj/F22 1 Tf-1.0476 -1.619 TD-0.0534 Tw(Implicit resource management and component life cycle.)Tj/F11 1 Tf27.7143 0 TD-0.0465 Tw(The EJB server)Tj-26.6667 -1.2381 TD0.0025 Tc-0.05 Tw(implicitly manages resources for your components, such as threads, sockets,)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.0091 Tw[(and database connections. The life cycle of the components themselves are)]TJT*0.0049 Tc0.0625 Tw(also managed, allowing for components to be reused by the EJB server as)TjT*0.0037 Tc[(necessary)-14.5(.)]TJ/F22 1 Tf-1.0476 -1.619 TD0.0023 Tc-0.0573 Tw(Implicit persistence.)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.4762 0 TD0.0025 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(Persistence is a natural requirement of any deployment)]TJ-9.4286 -1.2381 TD-0.05 Tw(that requires permanent storage. EJB offers assistance here by automatically)TjT*0.0004 Tc-0.0499 Tw(saving persistent object data to an underlying storage and retrieving that data)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0007 Tw(at a later time.)Tj/F22 1 Tf-1.0476 -1.619 TD-0.0411 Tw[(Implicit remote accessibility)94.7(.)]TJ/F11 1 Tf14.5714 0 TD-0.0358 Tw(EJB products will automatically convert your)Tj-13.5238 -1.2381 TD-0.0096 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(stand-alone, network-less components into distributed, network-aware beings.)]TJ/F22 1 Tf-1.0476 -1.619 TD-0.0011 Tc-0.0574 Tw(Implicit multiclient support.)Tj/F11 1 Tf14.0952 0 TD-0.0005 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(EJB servers automatically route concurrent re-)]TJ-13.0476 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc0.0456 Tw[(quests from clients. EJB servers provide built-in thread support, instantiat-)]TJT*0.0054 Tc0.0625 Tw(ing multiple copies of your component as necessary and channeling client)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.0005 Tw(requests to those instances.)TjETendstreamendobj251 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F15 22 0 R/F17 29 0 R/F22 81 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj253 0 obj<</Length 4272>>stream
