ote that the \322client\323 of an enterprise bean could be anything\321perhaps a servlet,)Tj0 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc-0.0445 Tw[(an applet, or even another enterprise bean. In the latter case, a client request to)]TJT*-0.0457 Tw(a bean can result in a whole chain of beans being called. This is a very powerful)TjT*-0.0317 Tw(idea because you can subdivide a complex bean task, allowing one bean to call)TjT*0.0002 Tw(on a variety of prewritten beans to handle the subtasks. This hierarchical con-)TjT*-0.0004 Tw(cept is quite extensible.)Tj/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 76 261 Tm0 Tc0.0003 Tw(Types of Beans)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 112 241 Tm0.0039 Tc0.0101 Tw(EJB 1.0 and 1.1 defines two different kinds of enterprise beans: )Tj/F13 1 Tf28.1905 0 TD(session)Tj/F11 1 Tf3.3333 0 TD0 Tc0 Tw( )Tj/F13 1 Tf0.2857 0 TD0.0039 Tc(beans)Tj/F11 1 Tf-31.8095 -1.2381 TD(and )Tj/F13 1 Tf1.9048 0 TD(entity beans)Tj/F11 1 Tf5.5238 0 TD[(. Let\325)39.3(s take a look at how they compare.)]TJ/F15 1 Tf11.5 0 0 11.5 112 197 Tm0.0119 Tc-0.0017 Tw(Session Beans)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 112 176 Tm0.0039 Tc-0.0064 Tw(A session bean represents work being performed for client code that is calling)Tj0 -1.2381 TD-0.0213 Tw[(it. Session beans are business process objects. They implement business logic,)]TJT*-0.0499 Tw[(business rules, and workflow)71.4(. For example, a session bean could perform price)]TJT*0.0088 Tc0.0625 Tw[(quoting, order entry)45.3(, video compression, banking transactions, stock trades,)]TJT*0.004 Tc0.0049 Tw(database operations, complex calculations, and more. They are reusable com-)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0002 Tw(ponents that contain logic for business processes.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD0.0393 Tw(Session beans are called session beans because they live for about as long as)Tj0 -1.2381 TD(the )Tj/F13 1 Tf1.7143 0 TD(session)Tj/F11 1 Tf3.3333 0 TD0.032 Tw[( \(or lifetime\) of the client code that\325)56.7(s calling the session bean. For)]TJ-5.0476 -1.2381 TD-0.0061 Tc-0.0496 Tw[(example, if client code contacted a session bean to perform order entry logic, th)-24.2(e)]TJT*0.0246 Tw[(application server \(that is, the EJB container/server\) is responsible for creating)]TJETendstreamendobj260 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F15 22 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj262 0 obj<</Length 4740>>stream
