ition to resource management, the EJB container is responsible for con-)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD-0.0234 Tw[(trolling the life cycle of the deployed enterprise bean components. As bean cli-)]TJT*0.0412 Tw[(ent requests arrive, the EJB container dynamically instantiates, destroys, and)]TJT*-0.0041 Tw(reuses beans as appropriate. For example, if a client requests a certain type of)TjT*-0.0013 Tc-0.05 Tw(bean that does not exist in memory yet, the EJB container may instantiate a new)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0419 Tw[(in-memory instance on behalf of the client. On the other hand, if a bean already)]TJT*0.0449 Tw[(exists in memory)33.2(, it may not be appropriate to instantiate a new bean\321espe-)]TJT*-0.0093 Tw[(cially if the system is low on memory)-11.1(. Instead, it might make more sense to re-)]TJT*0.0406 Tw[(assign a bean from one client to another)-28.2(. It might also make sense to destroy)]TJT*0.0002 Tw(some beans that are not being used anymore. This is called instance pooling.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD0.0587 Tw(The take-away point here is that the EJB container is responsible for coordi-)Tj0 -1.2381 TD-0.0114 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(nating the entire effort of resource management as well as managing the deployed)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0001 Tw[(beans\325 life cycle. Note that the exact scheme used is EJB container)40.4(-specific.)]TJ/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 67 171 Tm0.0002 Tc0.0012 Tw[(Stat)-19.2(e Management)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 150 Tm-0.0002 Tc-0.05 Tw[(State management is another value that containers bring to the table. To explain)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0214 Tw[(the need for state management, we first must observe that users, as well as cli-)]TJT*0.0107 Tw[(ent code, often take a lot of time to \322think\323 in between method calls to a com-)]TJT*-0.0144 Tw[(ponent. The classic example of this is an HTML \(W)40.6(eb\) client interacting with a)]TJT*0.0245 Tw[(human being. W)-9.1(eb users often will click on a button that executes some busi-)]TJT*-0.036 Tw[(ness logic in a component, but then they wait around and read text before initi-)]TJT*0.0159 Tw[(ating another action. While the user is doing this, the application server could)]TJT*-0.0002 Tw(reuse that component to service other clients.)TjETendstreamendobj294 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj296 0 obj<</Length 4622>>stream
