avigator window is open, perhaps connecting to an e-commerce)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0281 Tw[(site with deployed session beans. It could also be as long as your Java applet is)]TJT*0.0031 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(running, as long as a stand-alone application is open, or as long as another bean)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0005 Tw(is using your bean.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD-0.0436 Tw[(The length of the client\325)-27.3(s )]TJ/F13 1 Tf10.9524 0 TD(session)Tj/F11 1 Tf3.2381 0 TD[( generally determines how long a session bean)]TJ-14.1905 -1.2381 TD-0.0288 Tw(is in use\321that is where the term )Tj/F13 1 Tf14.381 0 TD-0.032 Tw(session bean)Tj/F11 1 Tf5.7143 0 TD-0.0288 Tw[( originated. The EJB container is)]TJ-20.0952 -1.2381 TD0.0414 Tw[(empowered to destroy session beans if clients time out. If your client code is)]TJT*0.0202 Tw[(using your beans for 10 minutes, your session beans might live for minutes or)]TJT*-0.0061 Tc-0.024 Tw[(hours, but probably not weeks, months, or years. T)16.4(ypically)103.3(,)-0.1( session beans do not)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0018 Tw(survive application server crashes, nor do they survive machine crashes. They)TjT*0.0002 Tw(are in-memory objects that live and die with their surrounding environments.)Tj0 -1.8095 TD0.0033 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(In contrast, entity beans can live for months or even years because entity beans)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc(are )Tj/F13 1 Tf1.7143 0 TD0.0569 Tw(persistent objects)Tj/F11 1 Tf7.9048 0 TD0.0512 Tw[(. Entity beans are part of a durable, permanent storage,)]TJ-9.619 -1.2381 TD-0.0122 Tw[(such as a database. Entity beans can be constructed in memory from database)]TJT*0 Tw(data, and they can survive for long periods of time.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD-0.0061 Tc-0.0314 Tw(Session beans are )Tj/F13 1 Tf7.9048 0 TD(nonpersistent)Tj/F11 1 Tf6.0952 0 TD(. This means that session beans are not saved to)Tj-14 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc-0.019 Tw[(permanent storage, whereas entity beans are. Note that session beans )]TJ/F13 1 Tf30.7619 0 TD(can)Tj/F11 1 Tf1.619 0 TD[( per)-22.7(-)]TJ-32.381 -1.2381 TD-0.0255 Tw[(form database operations, but the session bean )]TJ/F13 1 Tf20.8571 0 TD(itself)Tj/F11 1 Tf2.2857 0 TD[( is not a persistent object.)]TJ-23.1429 -1.8095 TD-0.0081 Tw(All session beans \(as well as entity beans\) must expose required )Tj/F13 1 Tf28.4762 0 TD(management)Tj-28.4762 -1.2381 TD-0.001 Tc-0.0555 Tw(callback methods)Tj/F11 1 Tf7.5238 0 TD-0.0005 Tc-0.0499 Tw(. The container uses the management methods to interact with)Tj-7.5238 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc0.0584 Tw[(the bean, calling them periodically to alert the bean to important events. For)]TJT*-0.0238 Tw[(example, the container will alert the bean when it is being initialized and when)]TJETendstreamendobj362 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj364 0 obj<</Length 11016>>stream
