2857 0 TD0.0059 Tc0.0626 Tw[(. Naming and directory services are products that store and look up re-)]TJ-2.2857 -1.2381 TD0.0087 Tc[(sources across a network. Some examples of directory service products are)]TJT*0.0132 Tc[(Netscape\325)14.9(s )]TJ/F13 1 Tf5.1429 0 TD0.0143 Tc0.0694 Tw[(Directory Server)]TJ/F11 1 Tf7.7143 0 TD0.0132 Tc0.0626 Tw[(, Microsoft\325)22.3(s )]TJ/F13 1 Tf5.9048 0 TD0.0143 Tc0.0694 Tw(Active Directory)Tj/F11 1 Tf7.619 0 TD0.0132 Tc0.0626 Tw[(, and IBM\325)102.7(s)0( )]TJ/F13 1 Tf5.4286 0 TD0.0142 Tc(Lotus)Tj-31.8095 -1.2381 TD0.0033 Tc(Notes)Tj/F11 1 Tf2.4762 0 TD0 Tc0 Tw(.)Tj-2.4762 -1.8095 TD0.0092 Tc0.0625 Tw[(T)48.8(raditionally)64.5(, corporations have used directory services to store usernames,)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc-0.013 Tw[(passwords, machine locations, printer locations, and so on. J2EE products ex-)]TJT*0.0063 Tc0.0626 Tw[(ploit directory services to store location information for resources that your)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0405 Tw[(application code uses in an enterprise deployment. These resources could be)]TJT*0.037 Tw[(EJB home objects, enterprise bean environment properties, database drivers,)]TJT*0.0037 Tc-0.0046 Tw(message service drivers, and other resources. By using directory services, you)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0245 Tw(can write application code that does not depend on specific machine names or)TjT*-0.0464 Tw[(locations. This is all part of EJB\325)38.8(s location transparency)30.7(, and it keeps your code)]TJT*0.0207 Tw[(portable. If later you decide that resources should be located elsewhere, your)]TJT*0.0073 Tc0.0626 Tw(code will not need to be rebuilt because the directory service can simply be)TjT*0.0039 Tc[(updated to reflect the new resource locations. This greatly enhances mainte-)]TJT*0.0107 Tw[(nance of a multi-tier deployment that may evolve over time. This becomes ab-)]TJT*0.0069 Tc0.0625 Tw(solutely necessary when purchasing prewritte