 is for a bean to)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0279 Tw(store client-specific data in a directory structure using JNDI. The client could)TjT*-0.0244 Tw(later pass the bean an identifier for locating the data in the directory structure.)TjT*0.0499 Tw[(This is quite similar to storing data in a database. The big difference is that a)]TJT*-0.0031 Tw(JNDI implementation could be an in-memory implementation \(this would give)TjT*-0.0128 Tw[(a similar effect to a shared property manager)11.8(, familiar to MTS/COM+ readers\).)]TJT*0.0001 Tw[(If client data is stored in memory)6.9(, there is no database hit.)]TJ0 -1.8095 TD-0.0086 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(When choosing between stateful and stateless, you should ask yourself what type)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0089 Tc0.0626 Tw[(of business process your session beans are attempting to emulate. Does the)]TJT*0.0035 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(business process span multiple invocations, requiring a conversation? If so, the)]TJT*0.0028 Tc[(stateful model fits very nicely because client-specific conversations can be part)]TJT*0.0038 Tc-0.0038 Tw(of the bean state. On the other hand, if your business process lasts for a single)TjT*-0.0001 Tw(method call, the stateless paradigm will better suit your needs.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD-0.0167 Tw[(In reality)34.7(, most sophisticated deployments are likely to have a complex and in-)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0208 Tc0.0626 Tw[(teresting combination of stateless and stateful beans. The choice between)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0307 Tw(stateful or stateless may also pale in comparison to other factors in your EJB)TjT*-0.044 Tw[(deployment, such as proper use of transactions. W)9.9(e)0(\325ll find out how to appropri-)]TJT*0 Tw(ately use transactions in Chapter 10.)TjET0.8 0.8 0.8 RG24 w 10 M /GS1 gs67 126 m97 126 lS0 0 0 RG1 w 67 114.5 m464 114.5 lSBT/F7 1 Tf15 0 0 15 73 120 Tm/GS2 gs-0.0002 Tc(Summary)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 91 Tm-0.016 Tc0.0017 Tw[(In this chapter, we learned how to program with stateful session beans. W)80(e)0.1( began)]TJT*0.0059 Tw[(with a look at the concepts behind stateful session beans and how they are differ)-32.2(-)]TJT*(ent )Tj1.619 0 TD0.0039 Tc-0.0198 Tw[(from stateless session beans. W)36.6(e)0( then coded up a simple counting program)]TJETendstreamendobj509 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj511 0 obj<</Length 983>>stream
