3 Tw(lowing code demonstrates using EJB object handles:)Tj/F24 1 Tf8 0 0 8 114 355 Tm-0.0003 Tc-0.0001 Tw(// First, get the EJB object handle from the EJB object.)Tj0 -1.375 TD(javax.ejb.Handle myHandle = myEJBObject.getHandle\(\);)Tj0 -2.75 TD0.0001 Tw(// Next, serialize myHandle, and then save it in)Tj0 -1.375 TD-0.0002 Tw(// permanent storage.)TjT*-0.0005 Tw(ObjectOutputStream stream = ...;)TjT*(stream.writeObject\(myHandle\);)Tj0 -2.75 TD0.0003 Tw(// time passes...)TjT*0.0002 Tw(// When we want to use the EJB object again,)Tj0 -1.375 TD-0.0005 Tw(// deserialize the EJB object handle)TjT*0.0001 Tw(ObjectInputStream stream = ...;)TjT*0.0006 Tw(Handle myHandle = \(Handle\) stream.readObject\(\);)Tj0 -2.75 TD-0.0001 Tw(// Convert the EJB object handle back into an EJB object)Tj0 -1.375 TD0.0001 Tw(MyRemoteInterface myEJBObject =)TjT*[(    )-92.7(\(MyRemoteInterface\) myHandle.getEJBObject\(\);)]TJ0 -2.75 TD0 Tw(// Resume calling methods again)Tj0 -1.375 TD(myEJBObject.callMethod\(\);)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 111 Tm-0.002 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(If you\325re using an EJB container based on Java RMI-IIOP \(see Chapter 11\) rather)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc0.0412 Tw[(than plain vanilla RMI \(see Appendix A\), you need to use the following state-)]TJT*0.0003 Tw(ment to convert the EJB object handle into an EJB object instead:)Tj/F24 1 Tf8 0 0 8 114 63 Tm-0.0003 Tc0.0002 Tw(// Convert the EJB object handle into an EJB object)Tj0 -1.375 TD0.0005 Tw(MyRemoteInterface myEJBObject = \(MyRemoteInterface\))TjETendstreamendobj547 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F17 29 0 R/F24 92 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj549 0 obj<</Length 4817>>stream
