etwork \(which is how Java RMI passes param-)TjT*-0.0015 Tw(eters over the network\), or you can save the stream to a storage, such as a file)TjT*0.0078 Tw[(system, database or JNDI tree. For sophisticated persistence, however)34.7(, object)]TJT*-0.0001 Tw(serialization falls short in many areas.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD-0.0061 Tc-0.0389 Tw[(For example, let\325)37.9(s say we store a million serializable bank account objects onto a)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.002 Tw(file system. We do this by converting the objects to their bit-blob representation)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.0243 Tw[(and then storing the bytes on disk. Let\325)-19.9(s say we then want to retrieve all bank)]TJT*0.0022 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(accounts that have balances over $1000. T)59(o)0( do this with serialization, we\325d have)]TJT*0.0009 Tc-0.05 Tw[(to load each and every bank account serialized bit-blob from the disk, construct)]TJT*0.0034 Tc[(the corresponding object, and then execute a method query on the object to de-)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0266 Tw[(termine if the balance is over $1000. W)39.3(e)0( might want to perform more advanced)]TJT*-0.0061 Tc0.006 Tw[(queries as well, such as retrieving all checking accounts that have been inactive)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0 Tw(for six months. There is no efficient way to do this with object serialization.)Tj0 -1.8095 TD-0.0002 Tw(In general, querying objects stored using object serialization is very expensive)Tj0 -1.2381 TD0.0409 Tw[(and cumbersome. Submitting queries against business data is an absolute ne-)]TJT*0.0107 Tc0.0625 Tw[(cessity for large-scale applications, which makes simple object serialization)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0303 Tw[(unsuitable for persistent storage. While object serialization has its purpose, it)]TJT*0.0051 Tc0.0625 Tw(is best used in restricted domains, such as for network communications and)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0006 Tw(simple persistence. For EJB, we\325ll need a more robust persistence mechanism)TjT*0.0004 Tw(to address more complex querying operations.)Tj/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 67 79 Tm0.0001 Tc-0.0008 Tw(Object-Relational Mapping)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 59 Tm-0.0061 Tc0.006 Tw[(Another popular way to store Java objects is to use a traditional relational data-)]TJT*0.0023 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(base, such as Oracle or Microsoft SQL Server)48.7(. Rather than serialize each object,)]TJETendstreamendobj653 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj655 0 obj<</Length 6923>>stream
