iting thread-safe code is difficult and error)-18.6(-)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0011 Tw(prone. Remember that the EJB value proposition is rapid application develop-)TjT*-0.0007 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(ment. Mandating that component vendors produce stable thread-safe code does)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0185 Tw[(not encourage this. Second, having multiple threads of execution makes trans-)]TJT*-0.0213 Tw(actions almost impossible to control by the underlying transaction system. Be-)TjT*-0.0061 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(cause of these reasons, EJB dictates that only a single thread can ever be running)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0136 Tw[(within a bean instance. With session beans, as well as entity beans, all bean in-)]TJT*0.0009 Tw(stances are single-threaded.)Tj0 -1.8095 TD0.0222 Tw(Mandating that each bean can service only one client at a time could result in)Tj0 -1.2381 TD-0.0048 Tc-0.05 Tw(performance bottlenecks. Because each instance is single-threaded, clients need)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0226 Tw[(to effectively run in lock-step, each waiting their turn to use a bean. This could)]TJT*0.0001 Tw(easily grind performance to a halt in any large enterprise deployment.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD-0.0133 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(T)26.3(o)0( boost performance, we could allow containers to instantiate multiple instances)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0005 Tc[(of the same entity bean class. This would allow for many clients to concurrently)]TJETendstreamendobj678 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj680 0 obj<</Length 4475>>stream
