ate in memory. Advanced EJB containers ship)]TJT*0.0069 Tc0.0625 Tw(with a shared object cache, which stores entity bean data in memory across)TjT*0.0029 Tc-0.05 Tw(transactions. Using a shared object cache, the container can avoid unnecessary)TjT*-0.0017 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(ejbLoad/ejbStore calls, which increases transactional throughput exponentially)14.7(.)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0054 Tw[(Note that you can cache entity bean state in memory using bean-managed per)-33.5(-)]TJT*-0.0001 Tw(sistence as well, but the burden of doing this falls on you.)Tj/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 67 266 Tm0.0002 Tc0 Tw[(Promise: Container-Managed P)-7(e)0(rsist)23.3(ence Reduces Bugs)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 245 Tm0.0039 Tc-0.0041 Tw[(One benefit of container)55.7(-managed persistence is that it eliminates many of the)]TJT*0.0255 Tw(bugs that occur in a deployment\321mostly due to buggy JDBC code. The prob-)TjT*-0.0054 Tw[(lem with JDBC code is that it\325)-18.1(s not \322type-safe.\323 Y)93.5(ou can\325)19(t detect whether it will)]TJT*0.0065 Tc0.0625 Tw[(work at compile time\321your JDBC statements are simple strings that can be)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0154 Tw[(resolved only at runtime. By way of comparison, with container)41.8(-managed per)-19.8(-)]TJT*-0.0087 Tw(sistence the EJB container has been written by a database professional whose)TjT*0.0064 Tw(sole job is to make sure the generated database calls are, in general, accurate.)TjT*-0.0048 Tc-0.05 Tw[(Plus, if you as a user have specified an error \(perhaps you misnamed a container)-33.5(-)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0117 Tw[(managed field in the deployment descriptor\), you )]TJ/F13 1 Tf21.9048 0 TD(can)Tj/F11 1 Tf1.619 0 TD[( detect errors at compile)]TJ-23.5238 -1.2381 TD0.0179 Tw[(time. The way you detect these errors is by running your EJB container tools,)]TJT*0.0169 Tw[(which, if they\325re any good, should use Java Reflection or the equivalent to fig-)]TJT*-0.0034 Tc-0.05 Tw[(ure out whether your deployment descriptor does indeed map to your container)-32.9(-)]TJT*-0.0023 Tc(managed fields. It can also check things such as whether your primary key fields)TjT*0.0038 Tc-0.0001 Tw(are a subset of your container-managed fields.)TjETendstreamendobj902 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F15 22 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj904 0 obj<</Length 4276>>stream
