nsac-)]TJT*0.0122 Tw[(tions are from one another)9.8(. Y)87.3(ou can enforce very strict isolation or allow very)]TJT*-0.0019 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(relaxed isolation. If you have very strict isolation, you can rest assured that each)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0286 Tw[(concurrent transaction will be isolated from all other transactions. But some-)]TJT*0.007 Tc0.0625 Tw(times enforcing strict isolation is a hindrance rather than a benefit. Because)TjT*0.0016 Tc-0.05 Tw(isolation is achieved by acquiring locks on an underlying data storage, the locks)TjT*0.0039 Tc0 Tw(can result in unacceptable performance degradation.)Tj0 -1.8095 TD-0.0051 Tw[(Thus, you need to be smart about how much isolation you really need. EJB of-)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0306 Tw(fers you different )Tj/F13 1 Tf8 0 TD0.034 Tw(isolation levels)Tj/F11 1 Tf6.7619 0 TD0.0306 Tw[( that give you this flexibility)34.4(. Isolation levels)]TJ-14.7619 -1.2381 TD0.0358 Tw(allow you to specify concurrency control at a very high level. If you specify a)TjT*-0.0439 Tw[(very strict isolation level, then your transactions will be perfectly isolated from)]TJT*0.0389 Tw(one another, at the expense of performance. If you specify a very loose isola-)TjT*0.0067 Tc0.0626 Tw[(tion level, your transactions will not be isolated, but you will achieve higher)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0006 Tw(concurrent transaction performance.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD0.0455 Tw[(T)43.5(ransaction isolation levels are attached to beans just like the transaction at-)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0121 Tc0.0626 Tw[(tributes we described earlier\321through the deployment descriptor)18.6(. The EJB)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0394 Tw(container knows how to inspect the deployment descriptor to apply the proper)TjT*-0.004 Tw(isolation levels to your beans. Figure 10.8 shows how we set a transaction iso-)TjT*0.0364 Tw[(lation level using BEA)27.6(\325)130.7(s)0( W)12(ebLogic deployment descriptor generation product.)]TJT*0.0003 Tw[(T)43.5(ransactio