)Tj-31.8095 -1.2381 TD0.0004 Tc(references)Tj/F11 1 Tf4.5714 0 TD0.0007 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(. An object reference is an identifier for a particular object implemen-)]TJ-4.5714 -1.2381 TD0.0061 Tc0.0626 Tw[(tation in CORBA. It uniquely identifies the object implementation across the)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0371 Tw[(network. An object reference automatically tracks the object implementation)]TJT*0.0009 Tw(it represents behind-the-scenes.)Tj0 -1.8095 TD0.0375 Tw[(Note that in theory)56.7(, you should not need to worry yourself with the details of)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD-0.0338 Tw[(object references\321you should just know that the ORB vendors use them inter)-32.7(-)]TJT*0.0132 Tw[(nally in their ORBs to identify objects. In reality)66.7(, each vendor\325)-24.4(s CORBA imple-)]TJT*-0.0055 Tc-0.05 Tw[(mentation deals with references in a slightly different way)39.3(,)0( and you have to know)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0001 Tw(how to get an object reference from each type of ORB.)Tj/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 67 259 Tm0.0002 Tc0.0006 Tw[(Object Adapt)-21.5(ers)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 239 Tm0.0024 Tc-0.05 Tw(A CORBA )Tj/F13 1 Tf4.4762 0 TD0.0022 Tc-0.0555 Tw[(object adapter)]TJ/F11 1 Tf6.2857 0 TD0.0024 Tc-0.05 Tw[( is a pluggable entity that assists in the following tasks:)]TJ/F20 1 Tf6 0 0 6 103 220 Tm0 Tc0 Tw(n)Tj0.5 0 TD(n)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 118 219 Tm0.0039 Tc(When an object is accessed, the object adapter is responsible for mapping)Tj0 -1.2381 TD0.0001 Tw(an object reference onto an object implementation behind the scenes.)TjT*0 Tw[(When a client performs an invocation, the ORB, the object adapter)21.8(, and)]TJT*0.0002 Tw(the implementation object coordinate to figure out which implementation)TjT*0.0005 Tw(object should be called.)Tj/F20 1 Tf6 0 0 6 103 151 Tm0 Tc0 Tw(n)Tj0.5 0 TD(n)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 118 150 Tm-0.0061 Tc0.0003 Tw[(If a client calls a method on an object implementation that is not 