IIOP)89.9(. This is shown in Figures 11.6 and 11.7.)]TJ-1.0476 -1.619 TD0 Tc( )Tj/F22 1 Tf0.2857 0 TD0.0039 Tc0.0236 Tw(A proprietary EJB server)Tj/F11 1 Tf12.4762 0 TD0.0206 Tw[( does not ship with a CORBA ORB. Rather)71.3(, it has)]TJ-11.7143 -1.2381 TD-0.0031 Tc-0.05 Tw(its own proprietary communications architecture. The proprietary EJB server)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.0302 Tw[(must still allow clients to call methods using RMI-IIOP API, because that is)]TJT*-0.0139 Tw[(mandated as of EJB 1.1. However)24.8(, the implementation of RMI-IIOP does not)]TJT*0.0088 Tc0.0625 Tw(use an ORB, and IIOP is not used as the transport protocol, which means)TjT*-0.0055 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(CORBA clients cannot call your enterprise beans. This is shown in Figure 11.8.)]TJETendstreamendobj1151 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F17 29 0 R/F22 81 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj1153 0 obj<</Length 8726>>stream
