n the server side. They know how to communicate with both the client, in HTTP)69.5(,)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0067 Tw[(and your enterprise beans, via RMI or IIOP)119.5(. This makes servlets the ideal tech-)]TJT*0.0005 Tw[(nology for W)41.8(eb-based GUI development.)]TJ/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 67 347 Tm0.0001 Tc-0.0002 Tw[(Alt)-19.9(e)-0.1(rnatives to Servlets)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 326 Tm-0.0168 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(There are other mechanisms for W)-28(eb-based communications as well. For example)23.1(,)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0014 Tw[(both Microsoft\325)-6.9(s Active Server Pages \(ASP\) and Sun\325)88.4(s Java Server Pages \(JSP\))]TJT*-0.0121 Tc-0.05 Tw[(provide a script-like environment for performing GUI operations. \(JSP is designed)]TJT*-0.0052 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(as a cross-platform solution; ASP is not, although there are cross-platform imple-)]TJT*0.0004 Tc(mentations that are unsupported by Microsoft.\) What advantages do these tech-)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.0001 Tw(nologies have over servlets?)Tj0 -1.9048 TD-0.0242 Tw[(T)43.5(o)0( answer this question, let\325)33.5(s take a deeper look at how servlets work. Servlets)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0247 Tw[(are compiled Java classes\321they are not script. When a servlet wants to write)]TJT*0.0002 Tw(HTML back to the client, it must make a method call, such as:)Tj/F24 1 Tf8 0 0 8 114 193 Tm-0.0003 Tc0.0011 Tw(response.write\("<B>Hi there</B>"\);)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 169 Tm0.0039 Tc0 Tw[(In ASP or JSP)79.6(, you\325d put the HTML directly into the script file itself:)]TJ/F24 1 Tf8 0 0 8 114 147 Tm-0.0003 Tc-0.0021 Tw(<B>Hi there</B>)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 103 123 Tm0.0039 Tc-0.0004 Tw[(W)35.8(ith servlets, you have the annoyance of having to code in a )]TJ/F13 1 Tf26.8571 0 TD(response.write\(\))Tj/F11 1 Tf-26.8571 -1.2381 TD-0.0042 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(whenever you want to send some UI text to the client. W)-54.7(i)-0.1(th JSP)186.9(, you simply write)]TJT*0.0064 Tc0.0625 Tw[