constructed because those objects referred to were also part)TjT*0.0274 Tw[(of the bit-blob. There\325s no danger of a reference being invalid after an invoca-)]TJT*0.016 Tc0.0625 Tw(tion because references are dynamically reconstructed in real time. This is)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0006 Tw(shown in Figure A.7.)Tj0 -1.8095 TD-0.0215 Tw[(Thus, object serialization assists Java RMI with the marshalling \(packaging\) of)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD-0.0051 Tw(parameters and the unmarshalling \(unpackaging\) of parameters. But serializa-)TjT*-0.0348 Tw[(tion has a wide variety of other purposes as well. For instance, object serializa-)]TJT*-0.0069 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(tion provides an instant file format for your objects. All you need to do is serialize)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0392 Tw[(them and write the serialized bit-blob to disk. It\325)44.3(s a quick and easy way to make)]TJT*0.0195 Tw[(your state persistent. For more information about Object Serialization, please)]TJT*0.0003 Tw[(see the book\325)20.7(s accompanying W)40.4(eb site.)]TJ/F7 1 Tf13.5 0 0 13.5 76 182 Tm0.0002 Tc0 Tw[(How R)-48(M)-45.8(I Simulat)20.4(e)0(s P)11.8(a)0(ss by Reference)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 112 162 Tm0.0039 Tc0.0442 Tw[(As we\325ve said, Java RMI relies on Object Serialization for passing parameters)]TJT*-0.0386 Tw[(via remote method invocations. The scenario we\325ve described is )]TJ/F13 1 Tf28.0952 0 TD-0.0429 Tw(pass by value)Tj/F11 1 Tf6 0 TD0 Tc0 Tw(,)Tj-34.0952 -1.2381 TD0.0067 Tc0.0625 Tw(where an entire graph of objects is serialized into a bit-blob, sent across the)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.0001 Tw(network, and then deserialized on the target machine.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD0.0188 Tw[(But passing parameters by value can lead to inefficiencies. What if your refer)-32.8(-)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD-0.0031 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(enced graph of objects is very large? What if you have lots of state to send across)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0132 Tw[(the network? The ensuing network lag from performing the invocation may be)]TJT*0.004 Tc(unacceptable.)TjETendstreamendobj1742 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F17 29 0 R/F20 77 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj1744 0 obj<</Length 11380>>stream
