e vendors can)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc-0.0367 Tw[(plug in. The SPI is the converse of the API: While the API allows clients to code)]TJT*0.0068 Tw[(to a single, unified interface, the SPI allows naming and directory service ven-)]TJT*0.0559 Tw(dors to fit their particular proprietary protocols into the system, as shown in)TjT*0.0397 Tw[(Figure B.2. This allows for client code to leverage proprietary naming and di-)]TJT*0 Tw[(rectory services in Java while maintaining a high level of code portability)9.6(.)]TJET0 0 0 0 k0 0 0 1 K1 j 0.88 w 3.864 M /GS3 gsq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm222.709 241.322 m297.814 241.322 l222.709 241.322 lbQq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm222.709 241.322 m297.814 241.322 l222.709 241.322 lbQq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm222.709 241.322 m297.814 241.322 l222.709 241.322 lbQ223.112 240.887 75.24 37.484 re223.112 278.371 m298.352 278.371 l298.352 240.887 l298.352 278.371 l223.112 278.371 lfq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm222.709 241.322 75.104 37.552 re222.709 278.874 m297.814 278.874 l297.814 241.322 l297.814 278.874 l222.709 278.874 lsQBT/F29 1 Tf7.495 0 0 7.468 235.652 257.348 Tm0 0 0 1 k-0.0002 Tc0.0001 Tw(Client code)TjET1 J [14.082 7.041 ]0 dq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm260.261 241.322 m260.261 175.606 lSQ[]0 dq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm255.567 188.905 m260.261 175.606 l264.173 188.905 lSQ0 0 0 0 kq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm138.217 100.501 m382.306 100.501 l138.217 100.501 lbQq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm138.217 100.501 m382.306 100.501 l138.217 100.501 lbQq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm138.217 100.501 m382.306 100.501 l138.217 100.501 lbQ138.467 100.32 244.53 37.484 re138.467 137.804 m382.997 137.804 l382.997 100.32 l382.997 137.804 l138.467 137.804 lfq1.0018 0 0 0.9982 0 0 cm138.217 100.501 244.089 37.552 re138.217 138.053 m382.306 138.053 l382.306 100.501 l382.306 138.053 l138.217 138.053 lsQBT7.495 0 0 7.468 204.302 116.781 Tm0 0 0 1 k[(Ser)-10.1(vic