 nine service providers for JNDI. Anyone)]TJT*-0.0381 Tw(can write a service provider\321and new ones will probably have emerged by the)TjT*-0.0004 Tw(time you read this.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD-0.0294 Tw[(Note that a service provider may not support every operation JNDI\325)22.9(s client API)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD-0.0432 Tw[(exposes. Each service provider ships with documentation that details the JNDI)]TJT*0.004 Tc-0.0097 Tw[(supported functions, as well as any specifics about the service provider. When)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0177 Tw[(you choose your service provider)-6.1(, see the included documentation for further)]TJT*0.004 Tc(details.)Tj/F15 1 Tf11.5 0 0 11.5 112 245 Tm0.0113 Tc[(LD)-52.8(AP)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 112 224 Tm0.0039 Tc-0.0198 Tw[(The Lightweight Directory Access Protocol \(LDAP\), invented at the University)]TJT*0.013 Tw[(of Michigan, was originally intended to be a ubiquitous protocol for accessing)]TJT*-0.0408 Tw[(directory services. Indeed, many directory services use LDAP as their standard)]TJT*0 Tw[(protocol. JNDI\325)-36.3(s value-add over basic LDAP is as follows:)]TJ/F20 1 Tf6 0 0 6 112 167 Tm0 Tc(n)Tj0.5 0 TD(n)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 127 166 Tm0.0039 Tc0.0002 Tw(JNDI is Java-based and provides Java clients with access to LDAP-based)Tj0 -1.2381 TD-0.0001 Tw(directories. Instead of using a custom LDAP package in Java, you can use)TjT*-0.0061 Tc-0.0002 Tw[(Sun Microsystem\325)33.3(s)0( LDAP service provider)63.4(, which is available free of charge.)]TJ/F20 1 Tf6 0 0 6 112 124 Tm0 Tc0 Tw(n)Tj0.5 0 TD(n)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 127 123 Tm0.0039 Tc(JNDI allows you to bind Java objects to directory structures \(which we\325ll)Tj0 -1.2381 TD-0.0002 Tw(see a bit later\).)Tj/F20 1 Tf6 0 0 6 112 94 Tm0 Tc0 Tw(n)Tj0.5 0 TD(n)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 127 93 Tm0.0039 Tc0.0002 Tw(The JNDI vision is to allow you to use other directory protocols besides)Tj0 -1.2381 TD0.0033 Tc[(LDAP)93(.)]TJ-1.4286 -1.9048 TD0.0039 Tc-0.0124 Tw[(Because LDAP is the most popular directory protocol, we\325ll use LDAP in some)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0068 Tc0.0626 Tw[(of the examples later in this appendix. The LDAP service provider from Sun)]TJETendstreamendobj1892 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F7 8 0 R/F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F15 22 0 R/F17 29 0 R/F20 77 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj1895 0 obj<</Length 4240>>stream
