 \(described in Chapter 11\), JNDI can be used)]TJT*0.0003 Tw(to bind RMI remote objects into the COS Naming Service.)Tj/F15 1 Tf11.5 0 0 11.5 112 347 Tm0.012 Tc0.0007 Tw[(File S)-36.5(ystem)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 112 326 Tm0.0039 Tc0.0008 Tw(The File System service provider gives you access to a file system through the)TjT*-0.0298 Tw[(JNDI client API. Y)59.4(ou can use the File System service provider to browse a hard)]TJT*-0.0323 Tw[(disk, for example, using JNDI operations. Clients can also store Java objects in)]TJT*0.0047 Tc0.0626 Tw[(the file system using JNDI. In a sense, when you use the File System service)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0131 Tw[(provider)41(, your file system itself is acting as a naming and directory service. W)45(e)]TJT*-0.0002 Tw(will demonstrate how to use this service provider later in this appendix.)Tj/F15 1 Tf11.5 0 0 11.5 112 230 Tm0.0119 Tc-0.0017 Tw[(R)-58.8(M)-27.6(I Registry)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 112 209 Tm0.0016 Tc-0.05 Tw(The RMI Registry service provider allows you to bind a whole RMI Registry into)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0019 Tw(a directory \(see Appendix A for an RMI tutorial\). The idea here is to bind your)TjT*0.0494 Tw[(RMI remote objects to a local RMI registry)-9.8(, then bind that registry to a direc-)]TJT*0.0006 Tc-0.05 Tw[(tory via JNDI. Clients can access your remote objects via JNDI rather than look-)]TJT*0.0084 Tc0.0626 Tw[(ing up objects in your RMI registry)70.4(. This allows multiple server machines to)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0005 Tw(publish their remote objects within a robust directory system, centralizing the)TjT*0.0515 Tw[(location of business objects. When clients use the regular RMI bootstrapping)]TJT*0.0019 Tc-0.05 Tw[(mechanism, they are connecting to individual servers that may)-22.7(,)0( in fact, be down)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0265 Tw[(at the time. W)30.1(ith the centralized directory system, clients can instead use JNDI)]TJT*-0.0079 Tw[(to find a list of available RMI registries. W)-17.3(e)0(\325ll explain more about how the RMI)]TJT*0.0464 Tw[(Registry service provider works, along with a complete example, later in this)]TJT*0.004 Tc[(chapter)28.6(.)]TJETendstreamendobj1899 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F11 10 0 R/F15 22 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj1901 0 obj<</Length 4459>>stream
