n mod-)TjT*0.0002 Tw(els these differently in its existing information systems.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD0.0029 Tc-0.05 Tw[(Unfortunately)54.3(, you\325re always going to need to write some workflow component)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.0027 Tc(that maps to each vendor\325s proprietary API and object model. The only way you)TjT*0.0039 Tc-0.0212 Tw(can get around mapping to APIs is if a standards committee decides on an offi-)TjT*0.0287 Tw[(cial object model for a problem domain, such as standardizing on what a pur)-32.5(-)]TJT*0.0115 Tc0.0626 Tw[(chase order looks like. Problem domains such as pricing are very open and)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0001 Tw(customizable, which makes this a very large challenge to overcome.)Tj0 -1.8095 TD0.0414 Tw[(There\325)39.5(s a second problem with having these components work together: data)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD-0.0024 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(mapping. How does the billing component understand the data computed by the)]TJT*0.0027 Tc-0.05 Tw[(pricing component? Sure, you might be able to call the billing component\325)12.8(s API,)]TJT*0.0016 Tc[(but it won\325)14.1(t magically know how to deal with the data passed to it. The data was)]TJT*0.0115 Tc0.0626 Tw[(formatted by another vendor\325)-14.8(s)0( component. Y)85.1(ou\325re going to need to write an)]TJT*0.0039 Tc0.0291 Tw[(adapter object that bridges the gap between the two formats. If you purchase)]TJT*0.0011 Tw(components from )Tj/F13 1 Tf8.0952 0 TD0 Tc0 Tw(n)Tj/F11 1 Tf0.6667 0 TD0.0039 Tc0.0011 Tw( vendors, you\325re going to be spending all your time writing)Tj-8.7619 -1.2381 TD0.0002 Tw(adapter code. This is quite mindless and boring.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD-0.0363 Tw[(XML has the potential to help with data mapping. Rather than application com-)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD0.058 Tw[(ponents sending proprietary data, components could interoperate by passing)]TJT*0.0089 Tc0.0626 Tw(XML documents as parameters. Because the data is formatted in XML, each)TjT*-0.0038 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(component could inspect the XML document to determine what data it received.)]TJ0 -1.8095 TD0.0039 Tc-0.0368 Tw[(XML must overcome several challenges before it reaches this level. One hurdle)]TJ0 -1.2381 TD-0.012 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(is performance. Parsing XML documents takes time, and sending XML documents)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0304 Tw[(over the wire takes even longer)46.9(. For high-performance enterprise applications,)]TJT*0.0053 Tc0.0625 Tw[(using XML at runtime for routine operations is very costly)26.7(. The performance)]TJT*0.0092 Tc0.0626 Tw[(barrier is slowly becoming a more trivial concern, however)30(, as XML parsers)]TJETendstreamendobj2092 0 obj<</ProcSet [/PDF /Text ]/Font <</F11 10 0 R/F13 18 0 R/F17 29 0 R>>/ExtGState <</GS1 11 0 R/GS2 12 0 R>>/ColorSpace <</CS2 30 0 R>>>>endobj2094 0 obj<</Length 4802>>stream
