n server is usually a fairly heavy-)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.01 Tw[(weight operation. If you\325re debugging an EJB application, having to restart the)]TJT*-0.0161 Tc-0.0034 Tw(EJB application server each time you regenerate your beans is a hassle. Having to)TjT*-0.0088 Tc-0.0499 Tw[(shut down an application server in order to deploy new beans has an even greater)]TJT*0.0039 Tc-0.0001 Tw(impact, since that application server cannot service clients when it is down.)Tj0 -1.8095 TD-0.0191 Tw(An enhanced value that some EJB products can provide above and beyond the)Tj0 -1.2381 TD0.0339 Tw[(EJB specification is a mechanism for deploying enterprise beans in real time.)]TJT*0.0126 Tw(This means the ability to deploy and re-deploy beans without shutting down a)TjT*-0.0004 Tw[(running application server)-14.2(.)]TJET0.8 0.8 0.8 RG24 w /GS1 gs76 183 m106 183 lS0 0 0 RG1 w 76 171.5 m473 171.5 lSBT/F7 1 Tf15 0 0 15 82 177 Tm/GS2 gs0.0002 Tc0.0005 Tw[(Distributed T)46.5(ransactions)]TJ/F11 1 Tf10.5 0 0 10.5 112 149 Tm0.0039 Tc-0.048 Tw[(In Chapter 10, we examined transactions in depth, and noted how multiple pro-)]TJT*-0.0024 Tc-0.05 Tw(cesses on different physical machines could participate in one large transaction.)TjT*0.0039 Tc0.0432 Tw(This is known as a )Tj/F13 1 Tf8.6667 0 TD0.048 Tw(distributed transaction)Tj/F11 1 Tf10.5714 0 TD0.0432 Tw(, and it is a fairly heavyweight op-)Tj-19.2381 -1.2381 TD0.0123 Tw[(eration. It necessitates the use of the )]TJ/F13 1 Tf16.5714 0 TD0.0137 Tw(distributed two-phase commit protocol)Tj/F11 1 Tf17.5238 0 TD0 Tc0 Tw(,)Tj-34.0952 -1.2381 TD0.0039 Tc0.0267 Tw(a reliable but cumbersome dance that transaction participants must take part)TjT*-0.0006 Tw(in for a distributed transaction to succeed.)Tj0 -1.9048 TD0.01 Tc0.0625 Tw(If you require distributed transactions, make sure your EJB server supports)Tj0 -1.2381 TD-0.0171 Tc-0.05 Tw(them. For a two-phase com